TITLE: foodcode-tomato
FCM: NON-DROP FRAME

001  AX       V     C        00:00:00:00 00:00:03:52 00:00:00:00 00:00:03:52
* FROM CLIP NAME: COOKED WRONG
* VISUAL: A tomato sitting on a kitchen counter with a red stamp reading COOKED WRONG
* NARRATION: Right now, there is a vegetable in your kitchen that you have been cooking wrong.

002  AX       V     C        00:00:03:52 00:00:07:28 00:00:03:52 00:00:07:28
* FROM CLIP NAME: MOST OF IT WASTED
* VISUAL: A tomato with its goodness spilling out through a hole in the bottom
* NARRATION: Not slightly wrong. Wrong in a way that throws away most of the benefit.

003  AX       V     C        00:00:07:28 00:00:11:04 00:00:07:28 00:00:11:04
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE OPPOSITE
* VISUAL: A health tips board with the rule crossed out and a reversing arrow
* NARRATION: And the fix is the opposite of what every health account has told you.

004  AX       V     C        00:00:11:04 00:00:14:09 00:00:11:04 00:00:14:09
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE RULE YOU KNOW
* VISUAL: A cookbook page reading cooking destroys nutrients with a big red X
* NARRATION: You have been told for years that cooking destroys nutrients in vegetables.

005  AX       V     C        00:00:14:09 00:00:17:29 00:00:14:09 00:00:17:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: BACKWARDS
* VISUAL: The same rule page flipped upside down with a backwards arrow
* NARRATION: For this one vegetable, that rule is not just wrong, it is backwards.

006  AX       V     C        00:00:17:29 00:00:20:35 00:00:17:29 00:00:20:35
* FROM CLIP NAME: MEASURED IN BLOOD
* VISUAL: A scientist with a pan of tomatoes beside a rack of blood sample tubes
* NARRATION: Researchers cooked tomatoes and measured exactly what happened in human blood afterward.

007  AX       V     C        00:00:20:35 00:00:23:40 00:00:20:35 00:00:23:40
* FROM CLIP NAME: 82%
* VISUAL: A blood tube with lycopene molecules rising and a gauge climbing
* NARRATION: The amount of lycopene in their blood rose by eighty two percent.

008  AX       V     C        00:00:23:40 00:00:27:16 00:00:23:40 00:00:27:16
* FROM CLIP NAME: ONLY WITH FAT
* VISUAL: Two pans side by side, one with oil rising, one flat lining
* NARRATION: But only when they cooked it with fat. Without fat, nothing happened at all.

009  AX       V     C        00:00:27:16 00:00:30:22 00:00:27:16 00:00:30:22
* FROM CLIP NAME: FLAT LINE
* VISUAL: A completely flat graph line stamped NO SIGNIFICANT INCREASE
* NARRATION: The group that cooked tomatoes without oil showed no significant increase whatsoever.

010  AX       V     C        00:00:30:22 00:00:33:42 00:00:30:22 00:00:33:42
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT A DIET BOOK
* VISUAL: A document with an official randomised controlled trial stamp on it
* NARRATION: That is not a diet book claim. That is a randomised controlled trial.

011  AX       V     C        00:00:33:42 00:00:36:47 00:00:33:42 00:00:36:47
* FROM CLIP NAME: STAY FOR THE NUMBER
* VISUAL: A finger pointing at a big bold number with a question mark beside it
* NARRATION: Stay until the end, because I will show you the exact number.

012  AX       V     C        00:00:36:47 00:00:39:53 00:00:36:47 00:00:39:53
* FROM CLIP NAME: TWO MISTAKES
* VISUAL: Two warning triangles labelled mistake one and mistake two
* NARRATION: And the two mistakes that almost everyone makes with this single vegetable.

013  AX       V     C        00:00:39:53 00:00:42:58 00:00:39:53 00:00:42:58
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT ABOUT EATING MORE
* VISUAL: A pile of vegetables with a person shrugging beside it
* NARRATION: This is not about eating more vegetables. You probably already eat enough.

014  AX       V     C        00:00:42:58 00:00:46:04 00:00:42:58 00:00:46:04
* FROM CLIP NAME: DOES IT REACH YOU
* VISUAL: Vegetables travelling down a tube toward a bloodstream, some bouncing off
* NARRATION: This is about whether the vegetables you eat actually reach your bloodstream.

015  AX       V     C        00:00:46:04 00:00:49:09 00:00:46:04 00:00:49:09
* FROM CLIP NAME: SWALLOWED VS ABSORBED
* VISUAL: Two doors, one reading swallowed and one absorbed, only one open
* NARRATION: Because there is a difference between swallowing a nutrient and absorbing it.

016  AX       V     C        00:00:49:09 00:00:52:14 00:00:49:09 00:00:52:14
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHERE ADVICE STOPS
* VISUAL: A finish line labelled the swallow with the science starting just behind
* NARRATION: Most health advice stops at the swallow. The science starts after it.

017  AX       V     C        00:00:52:14 00:00:55:50 00:00:52:14 00:00:55:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHAT'S COMING
* VISUAL: Three numbered boxes on a hand drawn title card
* NARRATION: Here is what I am going to show you, and it is genuinely simple.

018  AX       V     C        00:00:55:50 00:00:58:56 00:00:55:50 00:00:58:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE HIDDEN COMPOUND
* VISUAL: A tomato cut open revealing a hidden glowing molecule inside
* NARRATION: First, the compound hiding inside tomatoes that almost nobody talks about properly.

019  AX       V     C        00:00:58:56 00:01:02:01 00:00:58:56 00:01:02:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE MISTAKES
* VISUAL: Two big red X marks over everyday cooking habits
* NARRATION: Second, the two everyday mistakes that throw most of that compound away.

020  AX       V     C        00:01:02:01 00:01:05:07 00:01:02:01 00:01:05:07
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHAT IT DOES
* VISUAL: A body outline with the compound glowing as it travels inside
* NARRATION: Third, what it measurably does once it is actually inside your body.

021  AX       V     C        00:01:05:07 00:01:08:43 00:01:05:07 00:01:08:43
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE EXACT WAY
* VISUAL: A hand holding a tomato beside a checklist of numbered steps
* NARRATION: And I will give you the exact way to eat it, with real numbers.

022  AX       V     C        00:01:08:43 00:01:11:48 00:01:08:43 00:01:11:48
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT A SUPPLEMENT
* VISUAL: Supplement bottles and powder tubs crossed out, one tomato highlighted
* NARRATION: Not a supplement, not a powder, not a bottle with a label.

023  AX       V     C        00:01:11:48 00:01:15:24 00:01:11:48 00:01:15:24
* FROM CLIP NAME: ALREADY YOURS
* VISUAL: A tomato with a tick and the word free stamped across it
* NARRATION: The tomato you already own, prepared in a way you have probably never tried.

024  AX       V     C        00:01:15:24 00:01:18:44 00:01:15:24 00:01:18:44
* FROM CLIP NAME: LAST TIME
* VISUAL: A person at a table looking thoughtfully at a single tomato
* NARRATION: Think about the last time you ate a tomato. Really think about it.

025  AX       V     C        00:01:18:44 00:01:22:20 00:01:18:44 00:01:22:20
* FROM CLIP NAME: RAW ON A SALAD
* VISUAL: A sliced raw tomato on a salad plate, cold and firm
* NARRATION: Maybe it was sliced raw on a salad, cold and firm and slightly sour.

026  AX       V     C        00:01:22:20 00:01:25:56 00:01:22:20 00:01:25:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: STRAIGHT FROM THE PUNNET
* VISUAL: A hand eating cherry tomatoes straight from a punnet
* NARRATION: Maybe it was a few cherry tomatoes eaten straight from the punnet while cooking.

027  AX       V     C        00:01:25:56 00:01:29:17 00:01:25:56 00:01:29:17
* FROM CLIP NAME: FROM A JAR
* VISUAL: A jar of pasta sauce with a spoon resting in it
* NARRATION: Or maybe it was already cooked, in a pasta sauce from a jar.

028  AX       V     C        00:01:29:17 00:01:32:37 00:01:29:17 00:01:32:37
* FROM CLIP NAME: TOMATOES ARE HEALTHY
* VISUAL: A person giving a thumbs up beside a tomato with a halo
* NARRATION: You probably felt good about it. Tomatoes are healthy, everyone agrees on that.

029  AX       V     C        00:01:32:37 00:01:35:58 00:01:32:37 00:01:35:58
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHY IT'S MISSED
* VISUAL: A magnifying glass over a small hidden detail on a healthy tomato
* NARRATION: And they are. That is exactly why this is so easy to miss.

030  AX       V     C        00:01:35:58 00:01:39:18 00:01:35:58 00:01:39:18
* FROM CLIP NAME: ONE UNQUESTIONED RULE
* VISUAL: A rule book with one rule highlighted and no source cited
* NARRATION: Because we have absorbed one rule without ever questioning where it came from.

031  AX       V     C        00:01:39:18 00:01:42:23 00:01:39:18 00:01:42:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE THREE RULES
* VISUAL: Three rule cards, fresh, raw and cooking destroys, stacked up
* NARRATION: Fresh is better. Raw is better. Cooking destroys nutrients. End of discussion.

032  AX       V     C        00:01:42:23 00:01:45:29 00:01:42:23 00:01:45:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: TRUE FOR VITAMIN C
* VISUAL: A vitamin C molecule shrinking away in a hot pan
* NARRATION: That rule is true for vitamin C. Cooking really does destroy it.

033  AX       V     C        00:01:45:29 00:01:49:20 00:01:45:29 00:01:49:20
* FROM CLIP NAME: MINUS 29%
* VISUAL: A timer at thirty minutes with vitamin C dropping twenty nine percent
* NARRATION: Cook one for thirty minutes and you lose twenty nine percent of its vitamin C.

034  AX       V     C        00:01:49:20 00:01:52:41 00:01:49:20 00:01:52:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: RULE CONFIRMED
* VISUAL: A tick mark beside a measured loss on a chart
* NARRATION: So the rule feels confirmed. You measured the loss and you were right.

035  AX       V     C        00:01:52:41 00:01:55:46 00:01:52:41 00:01:55:46
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT THE REAL REASON
* VISUAL: A vitamin C badge crossed out, a lycopene molecule glowing larger beside it
* NARRATION: But vitamin C is not the real reason tomatoes are worth eating.

036  AX       V     C        00:01:55:46 00:01:58:52 00:01:55:46 00:01:58:52
* FROM CLIP NAME: SOMETHING WAS RISING
* VISUAL: A pan on heat with a rising arrow inside the tomato itself
* NARRATION: In that same thirty minutes, something else inside the tomato was increasing.

037  AX       V     C        00:01:58:52 00:02:02:28 00:01:58:52 00:02:02:28
* FROM CLIP NAME: PLUS 164%
* VISUAL: A big number one hundred sixty four percent with a red pigment molecule rising
* NARRATION: The compound that makes tomatoes red went up by one hundred sixty four percent.

038  AX       V     C        00:02:02:28 00:02:05:33 00:02:02:28 00:02:05:33
* FROM CLIP NAME: PLUS 62%
* VISUAL: An antioxidant meter climbing sixty two percent above a pan
* NARRATION: Total antioxidant activity in that same pan rose by sixty two percent.

039  AX       V     C        00:02:05:33 00:02:08:38 00:02:05:33 00:02:08:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: DOWN AND UP
* VISUAL: A see-saw with vitamin C going down and lycopene going up
* NARRATION: The vitamin went down, but the thing that actually matters went up.

040  AX       V     C        00:02:08:38 00:02:12:14 00:02:08:38 00:02:12:14
* FROM CLIP NAME: SOUNDS LIKE A TRICK
* VISUAL: A person stopping with a hand to ear, a speech bubble reading sounds like a trick
* NARRATION: That is the moment most people stop listening, because it sounds like a trick.

041  AX       V     C        00:02:12:14 00:02:16:06 00:02:12:14 00:02:16:06
* FROM CLIP NAME: JUST CHEMISTRY
* VISUAL: A chemistry flask with a tick, a magician's hat crossed out
* NARRATION: It is not a trick. It is chemistry, and it is very easy to understand.

042  AX       V     C        00:02:16:06 00:02:19:26 00:02:16:06 00:02:19:26
* FROM CLIP NAME: LYCOPENE
* VISUAL: A tomato wearing a name tag reading lycopene
* NARRATION: The red pigment in a tomato has a name. It is called lycopene.

043  AX       V     C        00:02:19:26 00:02:22:32 00:02:19:26 00:02:22:32
* FROM CLIP NAME: A CAROTENOID
* VISUAL: A molecule labelled carotenoid beside an empty vitamin bottle crossed out
* NARRATION: Lycopene is not a vitamin. It is a carotenoid, a pigment molecule.

044  AX       V     C        00:02:22:32 00:02:25:52 00:02:22:32 00:02:25:52
* FROM CLIP NAME: HIGHLY EFFICIENT
* VISUAL: A lycopene molecule on a podium among antioxidant contestants
* NARRATION: And it is one of the most efficient antioxidants found anywhere in nature.

045  AX       V     C        00:02:25:52 00:02:29:13 00:02:25:52 00:02:29:13
* FROM CLIP NAME: TEN TIMES
* VISUAL: Lycopene defeating ten free radical monsters while vitamin E handles one
* NARRATION: It neutralises more than ten times the free radicals that vitamin E handles.

046  AX       V     C        00:02:29:13 00:02:32:18 00:02:29:13 00:02:32:18
* FROM CLIP NAME: LOCKED INSIDE
* VISUAL: A lycopene crystal locked inside a cage of plant cell walls
* NARRATION: But inside a raw tomato, lycopene is locked in a crystalline prison.

047  AX       V     C        00:02:32:18 00:02:35:38 00:02:32:18 00:02:35:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOUR GUT CAN'T OPEN IT
* VISUAL: A padlocked crystal behind thick brick cell walls
* NARRATION: It sits inside rigid cell walls, packed in crystals your gut cannot open.

048  AX       V     C        00:02:35:38 00:02:38:59 00:02:35:38 00:02:38:59
* FROM CLIP NAME: A WELDED SAFE
* VISUAL: A safe with a welded door and banknotes visible through the gap
* NARRATION: Picture a safe with the door welded shut. The money is still inside.

049  AX       V     C        00:02:38:59 00:02:42:50 00:02:38:59 00:02:42:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: TRAPPED
* VISUAL: The safe with everything valuable trapped behind the welded door
* NARRATION: Everything of value is there, and none of it can get out to help you.

050  AX       V     C        00:02:42:50 00:02:46:11 00:02:42:50 00:02:46:11
* FROM CLIP NAME: SWALLOWING THE SAFE
* VISUAL: A person swallowing a whole safe instead of opening the door
* NARRATION: Eating that tomato raw is like swallowing the safe instead of opening it.

051  AX       V     C        00:02:46:11 00:02:49:47 00:02:46:11 00:02:49:47
* FROM CLIP NAME: STRAIGHT THROUGH
* VISUAL: Fibre, water and vitamin C passing through, lycopene bouncing away
* NARRATION: You get the fibre, the water, the vitamin C. The lycopene passes right through.

052  AX       V     C        00:02:49:47 00:02:53:23 00:02:49:47 00:02:53:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: HEAT OPENS IT
* VISUAL: A flame cracking rigid plant cell walls open like a nutcracker
* NARRATION: Heat is what opens the safe. It breaks those rigid plant cell walls apart.

053  AX       V     C        00:02:53:23 00:02:56:43 00:02:53:23 00:02:56:43
* FROM CLIP NAME: SOMETHING ELSE
* VISUAL: A surprised scientist with a shaking clipboard and an unexpected result
* NARRATION: And it does something else that nobody expected when they first measured it.

054  AX       V     C        00:02:56:43 00:03:00:19 00:02:56:43 00:03:00:19
* FROM CLIP NAME: TRANS AND CIS
* VISUAL: Two lycopene molecules, one straight one bent, labelled trans and cis
* NARRATION: Lycopene comes in two shapes, straight and bent. Scientists call them trans and cis.

055  AX       V     C        00:03:00:19 00:03:03:55 00:03:00:19 00:03:03:55
* FROM CLIP NAME: BENT ABSORBS BETTER
* VISUAL: A bent cis molecule slipping through the intestinal wall, the straight one stuck
* NARRATION: Your body absorbs the bent cis form far more easily than the straight one.

056  AX       V     C        00:03:03:55 00:03:07:16 00:03:03:55 00:03:07:16
* FROM CLIP NAME: HEAT FLIPS THEM
* VISUAL: Heat flipping straight molecules into bent ones like pancakes
* NARRATION: Cooking flips a meaningful share of the straight molecules into the bent shape.

057  AX       V     C        00:03:07:16 00:03:10:52 00:03:07:16 00:03:10:52
* FROM CLIP NAME: TWO JOBS
* VISUAL: One worker doing two jobs at once, freeing and reshaping
* NARRATION: So heat does two jobs at once. It frees the lycopene and reshapes it.

058  AX       V     C        00:03:10:52 00:03:14:43 00:03:10:52 00:03:14:43
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP ONE ONLY
* VISUAL: A staircase with step one marked and a warning sign further up
* NARRATION: But freeing it is only step one, and this is where most people still fail.

059  AX       V     C        00:03:14:43 00:03:18:04 00:03:14:43 00:03:18:04
* FROM CLIP NAME: FAT SOLUBLE
* VISUAL: Lycopene refusing to mix with water, dissolving happily in oil
* NARRATION: Lycopene does not dissolve in water. It dissolves in fat, and only fat.

060  AX       V     C        00:03:18:04 00:03:21:24 00:03:18:04 00:03:21:24
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE TRANSPORT
* VISUAL: Lycopene molecules boarding transport particles made of fat
* NARRATION: Your intestine absorbs it by packaging it into particles built from dietary fat.

061  AX       V     C        00:03:21:24 00:03:25:00 00:03:21:24 00:03:25:00
* FROM CLIP NAME: NO TRANSPORT
* VISUAL: A lycopene molecule with no vehicle watching the transport drive past
* NARRATION: No fat in the meal means no transport. The freed lycopene simply keeps going.

062  AX       V     C        00:03:25:00 00:03:28:05 00:03:25:00 00:03:28:05
* FROM CLIP NAME: 23 PEOPLE
* VISUAL: Twenty three people lined up in a trial room
* NARRATION: This was not assumed. It was tested directly on twenty three people.

063  AX       V     C        00:03:28:05 00:03:31:26 00:03:28:05 00:03:31:26
* FROM CLIP NAME: TWO GROUPS
* VISUAL: Two tables, one with an olive oil bottle and one without
* NARRATION: One group ate tomatoes cooked with olive oil. One group ate them without.

064  AX       V     C        00:03:31:26 00:03:35:17 00:03:31:26 00:03:35:17
* FROM CLIP NAME: PLUS 82%
* VISUAL: A blood chart with the olive oil group climbing eighty two percent
* NARRATION: The group that had olive oil saw their blood lycopene rise by eighty two percent.

065  AX       V     C        00:03:35:17 00:03:38:23 00:03:35:17 00:03:38:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT EVEN SMALL
* VISUAL: A flat line graph stamped no significant increase
* NARRATION: The group without oil showed no significant increase. Not a small one.

066  AX       V     C        00:03:38:23 00:03:41:59 00:03:38:23 00:03:41:59
* FROM CLIP NAME: P = 0.684
* VISUAL: A statistics board reading P equals zero point six eight four
* NARRATION: Nothing. The statistical result was a P value of zero point six eight four.

067  AX       V     C        00:03:41:59 00:03:45:35 00:03:41:59 00:03:45:35
* FROM CLIP NAME: IN PLAIN TERMS
* VISUAL: A plain language translation bubble reading as close to nothing as possible
* NARRATION: In plain terms, that is as close to no effect as research can report.

068  AX       V     C        00:03:45:35 00:03:48:55 00:03:45:35 00:03:48:55
* FROM CLIP NAME: THEY STACK
* VISUAL: Two mistake boxes stacked on top of each other
* NARRATION: So there are two mistakes, and they stack on top of each other.

069  AX       V     C        00:03:48:55 00:03:52:16 00:03:48:55 00:03:52:16
* FROM CLIP NAME: MISTAKE ONE
* VISUAL: A hand eating a raw tomato with lycopene still locked in cells
* NARRATION: Eat it raw and you never free the lycopene from the plant cells.

070  AX       V     C        00:03:52:16 00:03:55:36 00:03:52:16 00:03:55:36
* FROM CLIP NAME: MISTAKE TWO
* VISUAL: A pan with no oil, freed molecules escaping upward unabsorbed
* NARRATION: Cook it without fat and you free it, then fail to absorb it.

071  AX       V     C        00:03:55:36 00:03:58:56 00:03:55:36 00:03:58:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: EITHER ONE IS ENOUGH
* VISUAL: A single mistake knocking most of the benefit off a scale
* NARRATION: Either mistake on its own is enough to lose most of the benefit.

072  AX       V     C        00:03:58:56 00:04:02:02 00:03:58:56 00:04:02:02
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE NUMBER
* VISUAL: A big glowing number beside a video play button
* NARRATION: Now the number that convinced me this was worth a whole video.

073  AX       V     C        00:04:02:02 00:04:05:07 00:04:02:02 00:04:05:07
* FROM CLIP NAME: SAME DOSE
* VISUAL: Two plates holding the exact same measured dose of lycopene
* NARRATION: Researchers gave people the exact same dose of lycopene two different ways.

074  AX       V     C        00:04:05:07 00:04:08:28 00:04:05:07 00:04:08:28
* FROM CLIP NAME: FRESH VS PASTE
* VISUAL: Raw tomatoes on one side, tomato paste on the other, both with oil
* NARRATION: Once from raw fresh tomatoes, once from processed tomato paste. Both with fat.

075  AX       V     C        00:04:08:28 00:04:11:33 00:04:08:28 00:04:11:33
* FROM CLIP NAME: MEASURED FOR HOURS
* VISUAL: A clock with blood samples being taken hour after hour
* NARRATION: Then they measured the lycopene actually appearing in their blood over hours.

076  AX       V     C        00:04:11:33 00:04:15:09 00:04:11:33 00:04:15:09
* FROM CLIP NAME: 2.5 TIMES
* VISUAL: A bar chart with the paste peak towering two and a half times higher
* NARRATION: The paste group hit a peak two and a half times higher than fresh.

077  AX       V     C        00:04:15:09 00:04:18:14 00:04:15:09 00:04:18:14
* FROM CLIP NAME: NEARLY 4X
* VISUAL: An area chart showing nearly four times the shaded absorption
* NARRATION: Across the whole window they absorbed nearly four times more in total.

078  AX       V     C        00:04:18:14 00:04:21:20 00:04:18:14 00:04:21:20
* FROM CLIP NAME: SAME EVERYTHING
* VISUAL: Three identical labels, same food, same dose, same fat
* NARRATION: Same food. Same dose. Same fat. Almost four times the amount absorbed.

079  AX       V     C        00:04:21:20 00:04:24:40 00:04:21:20 00:04:24:40
* FROM CLIP NAME: AJCN 1997
* VISUAL: A journal cover reading American Journal of Clinical Nutrition, 1997
* NARRATION: That study was published in the American Journal of Clinical Nutrition in 1997.

080  AX       V     C        00:04:24:40 00:04:28:01 00:04:24:40 00:04:28:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: CROSSOVER TRIAL
* VISUAL: The same person swapping between two groups with a crossover arrow
* NARRATION: It was a crossover trial, so every participant served as their own control.

081  AX       V     C        00:04:28:01 00:04:31:21 00:04:28:01 00:04:31:21
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE TELL
* VISUAL: A magnifying glass over one small detail in the data table
* NARRATION: And here is the detail that tells you this is real and specific.

082  AX       V     C        00:04:31:21 00:04:34:26 00:04:31:21 00:04:34:26
* FROM CLIP NAME: THEY CHECKED OTHERS
* VISUAL: Other carotenoid molecules being measured alongside the lycopene
* NARRATION: They also measured the other carotenoids present in those same blood samples.

083  AX       V     C        00:04:34:26 00:04:37:32 00:04:34:26 00:04:37:32
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE OTHERS FLAT
* VISUAL: Alpha and beta carotene each with a flat line graph
* NARRATION: Alpha carotene and beta carotene both showed no significant difference at all.

084  AX       V     C        00:04:37:32 00:04:40:52 00:04:37:32 00:04:40:52
* FROM CLIP NAME: SPECIFIC TO LYCOPENE
* VISUAL: A crystal structure with a target on it, everything else greyed out
* NARRATION: The effect was specific to lycopene and the crystal structure it sits in.

085  AX       V     C        00:04:40:52 00:04:43:58 00:04:40:52 00:04:43:58
* FROM CLIP NAME: REAL VS HEADLINE
* VISUAL: A real finding badge beside a crumpled nutrition headline
* NARRATION: That specificity is what separates a real finding from a nutrition headline.

086  AX       V     C        00:04:43:58 00:04:47:18 00:04:43:58 00:04:47:18
* FROM CLIP NAME: SURPRISED THEM TOO
* VISUAL: A researcher with wide eyes and a clipboard slipping from their hands
* NARRATION: Now here is the part that surprised even the researchers who ran it.

087  AX       V     C        00:04:47:18 00:04:50:23 00:04:47:18 00:04:50:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: IT PICKS SPOTS
* VISUAL: A body map with lycopene gathering unevenly in specific organs
* NARRATION: Lycopene does not float around evenly once it is in your body.

088  AX       V     C        00:04:50:23 00:04:53:29 00:04:50:23 00:04:53:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOUR SKIN
* VISUAL: A cross-section of skin with lycopene molecules settling into it
* NARRATION: It accumulates in specific tissues, and one of them is your skin.

089  AX       V     C        00:04:53:29 00:04:56:34 00:04:53:29 00:04:56:34
* FROM CLIP NAME: SOUNDS IMPOSSIBLE
* VISUAL: A research team pointing at an impossible looking question mark
* NARRATION: So a team of researchers decided to test something that sounds impossible.

090  AX       V     C        00:04:56:34 00:04:59:40 00:04:56:34 00:04:59:40
* FROM CLIP NAME: FOOD AS SUNBLOCK
* VISUAL: Sun rays hitting an arm with a question mark and a tomato beside it
* NARRATION: Could eating a food change how badly your skin burns in sunlight?

091  AX       V     C        00:04:59:40 00:05:03:00 00:04:59:40 00:05:03:00
* FROM CLIP NAME: 40G A DAY
* VISUAL: Nine volunteers each eating forty grams of tomato paste daily
* NARRATION: Nine volunteers ate forty grams of tomato paste every day for ten weeks.

092  AX       V     C        00:05:03:00 00:05:06:05 00:05:03:00 00:05:06:05
* FROM CLIP NAME: 16 MG
* VISUAL: A spoon of tomato paste labelled sixteen milligrams beside olive oil
* NARRATION: That is about sixteen milligrams of lycopene, always eaten with olive oil.

093  AX       V     C        00:05:06:05 00:05:09:41 00:05:06:05 00:05:09:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE CONTROL GROUP
* VISUAL: Ten other people with olive oil only and an empty tomato paste bowl
* NARRATION: Ten other people ate the same olive oil and no tomato paste at all.

094  AX       V     C        00:05:09:41 00:05:12:47 00:05:09:41 00:05:12:47
* FROM CLIP NAME: CONTROLLED UV
* VISUAL: A solar simulator lamp shining UV onto a patch of back skin
* NARRATION: Then researchers shone a controlled dose of ultraviolet light on their skin.

095  AX       V     C        00:05:12:47 00:05:16:07 00:05:12:47 00:05:16:07
* FROM CLIP NAME: 40% LESS RED
* VISUAL: Two skin patches side by side, one clearly forty percent less red
* NARRATION: The tomato paste group developed forty percent less redness than the control group.

096  AX       V     C        00:05:16:07 00:05:19:13 00:05:16:07 00:05:19:13
* FROM CLIP NAME: FORTY PERCENT
* VISUAL: A big forty percent badge with a sun and a tomato together
* NARRATION: Forty percent less sunburn, measured, from eating a food for ten weeks.

097  AX       V     C        00:05:19:13 00:05:22:33 00:05:19:13 00:05:22:33
* FROM CLIP NAME: J NUTR 2001
* VISUAL: A journal cover reading Journal of Nutrition, 2001
* NARRATION: That study ran in the Journal of Nutrition in two thousand and one.

098  AX       V     C        00:05:22:33 00:05:25:38 00:05:22:33 00:05:25:38
* FROM CLIP NAME: REPEATED
* VISUAL: Twenty women in a twelve week randomised trial calendar
* NARRATION: A later randomised trial repeated it in twenty women over twelve weeks.

099  AX       V     C        00:05:25:38 00:05:28:44 00:05:25:38 00:05:28:44
* FROM CLIP NAME: DEEPER DAMAGE TOO
* VISUAL: Skin layers with protection shields at two different depths
* NARRATION: It found protection not just from redness, but from deeper damage too.

100  AX       V     C        00:05:28:44 00:05:31:49 00:05:28:44 00:05:31:49
* FROM CLIP NAME: MATRIX AND DNA
* VISUAL: A skin matrix grid and a mitochondrial DNA strand both shielded
* NARRATION: Changes in the skin's structural matrix, and damage to mitochondrial DNA itself.

101  AX       V     C        00:05:31:49 00:05:35:10 00:05:31:49 00:05:35:10
* FROM CLIP NAME: BEING HONEST
* VISUAL: An honest weighing scale with a hand holding one side down
* NARRATION: Now I need to be completely honest with you about the scale here.

102  AX       V     C        00:05:35:10 00:05:38:15 00:05:35:10 00:05:38:15
* FROM CLIP NAME: SPF 1.3
* VISUAL: A tiny SPF one point three badge beside a huge SPF thirty bottle
* NARRATION: That protection works out to roughly an SPF of one point three.

103  AX       V     C        00:05:38:15 00:05:41:20 00:05:38:15 00:05:41:20
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT SUNSCREEN
* VISUAL: A dermatologist pointing at SPF thirty, tomato paste crossed out as sunscreen
* NARRATION: Dermatologists recommend a factor of thirty or higher. This is not sunscreen.

104  AX       V     C        00:05:41:20 00:05:44:41 00:05:41:20 00:05:44:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: SLOW AND SMALL
* VISUAL: A small shield growing slowly across a calendar of months
* NARRATION: It is a small basal layer of protection that builds slowly over months.

105  AX       V     C        00:05:44:41 00:05:48:17 00:05:44:41 00:05:48:17
* FROM CLIP NAME: TEN WEEKS
* VISUAL: A calendar showing week four no difference and week ten protection
* NARRATION: And it took ten weeks to appear. At week four there was no difference.

106  AX       V     C        00:05:48:17 00:05:51:37 00:05:48:17 00:05:51:37
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE HEART ANGLE
* VISUAL: A cardiologist with a heart and a blood pressure cuff
* NARRATION: There is a third thing, and it is the one cardiologists care about.

107  AX       V     C        00:05:51:37 00:05:54:43 00:05:51:37 00:05:54:43
* FROM CLIP NAME: SIX TRIALS
* VISUAL: Six trial documents being pooled into one analysis
* NARRATION: A pooled analysis of six controlled trials looked directly at blood pressure.

108  AX       V     C        00:05:54:43 00:05:57:48 00:05:54:43 00:05:57:48
* FROM CLIP NAME: MINUS 5 MMHG
* VISUAL: A blood pressure gauge with the systolic number dropping about five points
* NARRATION: Systolic pressure dropped by an average of about five millimetres of mercury.

109  AX       V     C        00:05:57:48 00:06:00:53 00:05:57:48 00:06:00:53
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE TOP NUMBER
* VISUAL: A blood pressure reading with the top number highlighted beside stiff arteries
* NARRATION: That is the top number, the one that rises as arteries stiffen.

110  AX       V     C        00:06:00:53 00:06:03:59 00:06:00:53 00:06:03:59
* FROM CLIP NAME: ONLY IF ELEVATED
* VISUAL: A high gauge improving while a normal gauge stays flat
* NARRATION: But it only appeared in people whose blood pressure was already elevated.

111  AX       V     C        00:06:03:59 00:06:07:04 00:06:03:59 00:06:07:04
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT IF YOU'RE NORMAL
* VISUAL: A normal blood pressure gauge stamped no change
* NARRATION: In people with already normal pressure, lycopene did essentially nothing at all.

112  AX       V     C        00:06:07:04 00:06:10:40 00:06:07:04 00:06:10:40
* FROM CLIP NAME: WHO IT'S FOR
* VISUAL: A signpost pointing to exactly who this helps
* NARRATION: Which is honest and useful, because it tells you who this is actually for.

113  AX       V     C        00:06:10:40 00:06:13:46 00:06:10:40 00:06:13:46
* FROM CLIP NAME: ABOVE 12 MG
* VISUAL: A dose scale with twelve milligrams marked as the threshold
* NARRATION: Daily doses above twelve milligrams worked noticeably better than the smaller doses.

114  AX       V     C        00:06:13:46 00:06:16:51 00:06:13:46 00:06:16:51
* FROM CLIP NAME: FOUR STEPS
* VISUAL: A title card with four numbered boxes in hand drawn capitals
* NARRATION: So what do you actually do with all of this? Four things.

115  AX       V     C        00:06:16:51 00:06:19:56 00:06:16:51 00:06:19:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP ONE: COOK THEM
* VISUAL: Step one card beside a pan of tomatoes cooking properly
* NARRATION: Simple, specific, and all of them free. Step one, cook your tomatoes.

116  AX       V     C        00:06:19:56 00:06:23:17 00:06:19:56 00:06:23:17
* FROM CLIP NAME: IN A PAN
* VISUAL: A pan with tomatoes breaking down gently, a boiling pot crossed out
* NARRATION: Not boiled to death. Cooked properly, in a pan, until they break down.

117  AX       V     C        00:06:23:17 00:06:26:22 00:06:23:17 00:06:26:22
* FROM CLIP NAME: 20 TO 30 MINUTES
* VISUAL: A timer at twenty to thirty minutes beside a rising graph
* NARRATION: Twenty to thirty minutes is where the research found the biggest increase.

118  AX       V     C        00:06:26:22 00:06:29:28 00:06:26:22 00:06:29:28
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP TWO: ADD FAT
* VISUAL: Step two card with olive oil pouring into the pan
* NARRATION: Step two, cook them with fat. Olive oil is the obvious choice.

119  AX       V     C        00:06:29:28 00:06:32:48 00:06:29:28 00:06:32:48
* FROM CLIP NAME: FREED THEN LOST
* VISUAL: A fat free pan with freed molecules escaping upward and away
* NARRATION: Without fat in the same meal, you free the lycopene and lose it.

120  AX       V     C        00:06:32:48 00:06:35:53 00:06:32:48 00:06:35:53
* FROM CLIP NAME: CHEMISTRY, NOT OPINION
* VISUAL: A chemistry flask with a tick, a chef's hat crossed out
* NARRATION: This is genuine chemistry, not a preference and not a chef's opinion.

121  AX       V     C        00:06:35:53 00:06:38:59 00:06:35:53 00:06:38:59
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP THREE: PROCESSED
* VISUAL: Step three card with tomato paste, passata and tinned tomatoes on a shelf
* NARRATION: Step three, choose processed tomato products when you can. Paste, passata, tinned.

122  AX       V     C        00:06:38:59 00:06:42:19 00:06:38:59 00:06:42:19
* FROM CLIP NAME: PASTE WINS
* VISUAL: Tomato paste on a podium ahead of fresh tomatoes, four to one
* NARRATION: The paste in the absorption study beat fresh tomatoes by nearly four times.

123  AX       V     C        00:06:42:19 00:06:45:25 00:06:42:19 00:06:45:25
* FROM CLIP NAME: MEASURED, NOT MARKETED
* VISUAL: A marketing megaphone crossed out beside a blood sample with a tick
* NARRATION: That is not marketing talk. It was measured directly in human blood.

124  AX       V     C        00:06:45:25 00:06:48:30 00:06:45:25 00:06:48:30
* FROM CLIP NAME: TINNED COUNTS
* VISUAL: A tin of tomatoes and a jar of passata both with ticks
* NARRATION: Tinned tomatoes count too, and so does a decent jar of passata.

125  AX       V     C        00:06:48:30 00:06:51:50 00:06:48:30 00:06:51:50
* FROM CLIP NAME: STEP FOUR: EAT BOTH
* VISUAL: Step four card with a tomato half raw and half cooked
* NARRATION: Step four, keep eating some raw as well. This is not either or.

126  AX       V     C        00:06:51:50 00:06:54:56 00:06:51:50 00:06:54:56
* FROM CLIP NAME: KEEP THE VITAMIN C
* VISUAL: A raw tomato wearing a vitamin C badge
* NARRATION: Raw tomatoes still give you the vitamin C that cooking partly destroys.

127  AX       V     C        00:06:54:56 00:06:58:16 00:06:54:56 00:06:58:16
* FROM CLIP NAME: BOTH
* VISUAL: Two plates side by side, cooked with fat and raw, both ticked
* NARRATION: So eat both. Cooked with fat for lycopene, raw for the vitamin C.

128  AX       V     C        00:06:58:16 00:07:01:52 00:06:58:16 00:07:01:52
* FROM CLIP NAME: ONE DAY, BOTH WAYS
* VISUAL: A salad with raw tomato and olive oil beside a bowl of cooked sauce
* NARRATION: A salad with raw tomato and olive oil, plus a cooked sauce at dinner.

129  AX       V     C        00:07:01:52 00:07:04:58 00:07:01:52 00:07:04:58
* FROM CLIP NAME: TWO COMPOUNDS COVERED
* VISUAL: One plate covering both compounds with two satisfied ticks
* NARRATION: That single combination covers both compounds without you thinking about it again.

130  AX       V     C        00:07:04:58 00:07:08:18 00:07:04:58 00:07:08:18
* FROM CLIP NAME: A LONG GAME
* VISUAL: A calendar with ten weeks marked and a slow moving turtle
* NARRATION: And if you want the skin effect, understand it is a long game.

131  AX       V     C        00:07:08:18 00:07:11:23 00:07:08:18 00:07:11:23
* FROM CLIP NAME: NOT A QUICK FIX
* VISUAL: A beach holiday one week away crossed out, ten weeks ticked
* NARRATION: Ten weeks of daily intake. Not a week before a beach holiday.

132  AX       V     C        00:07:11:23 00:07:14:29 00:07:11:23 00:07:14:29
* FROM CLIP NAME: IT'S ALL PUBLISHED
* VISUAL: A tall stack of published nutrition papers on a desk
* NARRATION: All of this is sitting in the published nutrition literature right now.

133  AX       V     C        00:07:14:29 00:07:17:49 00:07:14:29 00:07:17:49
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE GAP
* VISUAL: A research paper on one side, a home kitchen on the other, a wide gap
* NARRATION: But almost nobody translates it into something you can use in a kitchen.

134  AX       V     C        00:07:17:49 00:07:21:25 00:07:17:49 00:07:21:25
* FROM CLIP NAME: THE MISSION
* VISUAL: A bridge labelled Food Code spanning from the paper to the pan
* NARRATION: That gap between the paper and your pan is what Food Code is for.

135  AX       V     C        00:07:21:25 00:07:25:01 00:07:21:25 00:07:25:01
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU CHANGED
* VISUAL: A person transformed, glowing brain, looking thoughtfully at a tomato
* NARRATION: After today you are not someone who just eats tomatoes because they are healthy.

136  AX       V     C        00:07:25:01 00:07:28:37 00:07:25:01 00:07:28:37
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU KNOW ITS NAME
* VISUAL: A name tag on a red pigment molecule and a locked crystal
* NARRATION: You know the pigment has a name, and you know it is locked inside.

137  AX       V     C        00:07:28:37 00:07:32:13 00:07:28:37 00:07:32:13
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU KNOW THE MECHANISM
* VISUAL: Heat cracking cell walls and flipping molecules into bent shapes
* NARRATION: You know heat opens the walls and flips the molecule into its bent shape.

138  AX       V     C        00:07:32:13 00:07:35:49 00:07:32:13 00:07:35:49
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU KNOW THE TRANSPORT
* VISUAL: A fat transport truck carrying lycopene, an empty road without it
* NARRATION: You know fat is the transport, and without it the whole thing is wasted.

139  AX       V     C        00:07:35:49 00:07:39:10 00:07:35:49 00:07:39:10
* FROM CLIP NAME: RAW ISN'T AUTOMATICALLY BETTER
* VISUAL: A raw tomato stamped not automatically better, an arrow pointing down
* NARRATION: And you know that raw is not automatically better. Sometimes it is worse.

140  AX       V     C        00:07:39:10 00:07:42:15 00:07:39:10 00:07:42:15
* FROM CLIP NAME: EVERY TOMATO AFTER THIS
* VISUAL: A pan with every future tomato being cooked the new way
* NARRATION: That one idea changes how you cook every tomato from now on.

141  AX       V     C        00:07:42:15 00:07:45:35 00:07:42:15 00:07:45:35
* FROM CLIP NAME: TELL ME
* VISUAL: A comment box with three tomato options and a reply badge
* NARRATION: Tell me in the comments how you eat tomatoes. Raw, cooked, or both.

142  AX       V     C        00:07:45:35 00:07:48:41 00:07:45:35 00:07:48:41
* FROM CLIP NAME: I READ THEM
* VISUAL: A stack of comment cards with reply badges and a ready pen
* NARRATION: I read every single one, and I reply to the interesting ones.

143  AX       V     C        00:07:48:41 00:07:52:17 00:07:48:41 00:07:52:17
* FROM CLIP NAME: NEXT VIDEO
* VISUAL: A mystery vegetable under a spotlight with a question mark
* NARRATION: In the next video I am going after another vegetable we all cook wrong.

144  AX       V     C        00:07:52:17 00:07:55:22 00:07:52:17 00:07:55:22
* FROM CLIP NAME: OVERCOOKED
* VISUAL: A kitchen counter with the mystery vegetable, shrivelled and overcooked
* NARRATION: It is in your kitchen right now, and almost everyone overcooks it.

145  AX       V     C        00:07:55:22 00:07:58:28 00:07:55:22 00:07:58:28
* FROM CLIP NAME: YOU KNOW THIS ONE
* VISUAL: The mystery vegetable with a famous compound name fading in behind it
* NARRATION: And the compound it destroys is one you have definitely heard of.

